---
components: ["Scheduler"]
description: Schedulers show events on a day, week or month calendar, and let people create, move and resize them with the pointer or the keyboard.
---

<script>
  import { Scheduler } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  // Times are UTC so each example reads the same for every visitor.
  const at = (day, hour, minute = 0) =>
    new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 9, 26 + day, hour, minute));

  const events = [
    { id: 1, title: "Incident review", start: at(0, 9), end: at(0, 10), color: "red" },
    { id: 2, title: "Capacity planning", start: at(1, 10), end: at(1, 11, 30), color: "purple" },
    { id: 3, title: "us-south rollout", start: at(1, 10, 30), end: at(1, 12), color: "teal" },
    { id: 4, title: "Quarterly planning", start: at(2, 0), end: at(5, 0), allDay: true, color: "cyan" },
    { id: 5, title: "On-call: platform", start: at(3, 14), end: at(3, 15), color: "green" },
    { id: 6, title: "Release night", start: at(4, 22), end: at(5, 2), color: "magenta" },
  ];

  const dstEvents = [
    // 01:30 EDT to 01:30 EST: one hour passes while the wall clock reads the same.
    { id: 1, title: "Backup", start: new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 10, 1, 5, 30)), end: new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 10, 1, 6, 30)), color: "teal" },
    // 00:30 EDT to 03:30 EST: four hours pass on a 25-hour day.
    { id: 2, title: "Maintenance", start: new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 10, 1, 4, 30)), end: new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 10, 1, 8, 30)), color: "purple" },
  ];
</script>

## Basic

Pass `events` and a `date`. Each event takes a unique `id`, a `title`, a `start` and an `end`, which are `Date`s. The week view shows the week that holds `date`, scrolled to `scrollHour`.

`end` is exclusive, as in iCalendar and Google Calendar: a meeting from 10:00 to 11:00 has an `end` of 11:00, and an all-day event on Monday has an `end` of Tuesday's midnight. An event without an `end` lasts no time, or one day when it is all-day, and the grid shows it one slot tall.

Use `bind:view` and `bind:date` to read or set the view and the date. `bind:events` keeps the array in step when the user moves or resizes an event; see [Change events](#change-events).

<FileSource src="/framed/Scheduler/SchedulerBasic" />

## Views

Set `view` to `"day"`, `"week"` or `"month"`. The toolbar switches views and steps through time; set `toolbar` to `false` to hide it and drive `view` and `date` yourself.

### Day

<Scheduler {events} view="day" date={at(1, 12)} timeZone="UTC" height="22rem" />

### Month

The month view shows each week as a row. Events that cover whole days run across the row as bars, and timed events show as a dot and a line of text. A day that has more than `monthEventLimit` lines (default `3`) ends with a "+N more" link, which opens that day. Its name adds the date, such as "+2 more events on Tuesday, October 27, 2026"; change it with `moreLabelText`. Clicking a day number opens the day too.

<Scheduler {events} view="month" date={at(2, 12)} timeZone="UTC" height="30rem" />

## Events

### All-day and multi-day

Set `allDay` to show an event in the all-day row. A timed event that lasts 24 hours or more also goes in the all-day row, as in Google Calendar and Outlook, and keeps its times in the label. A timed event shorter than 24 hours that crosses midnight is split in the day and week views: each day shows its own part, with a dashed edge where it continues. The month view shows it on the day it starts.

### Overlapping

Events that overlap sit side by side, as in Google Calendar. An event grows into lanes that nothing else uses at its time, so a lone meeting beside a busy hour fills the row. An event shorter than one slot renders one slot tall, and the layout counts that height, so text never overlaps.

### Colors

Set `color` to one of the Carbon tag colors: `"gray"`, `"red"`, `"magenta"`, `"purple"`, `"blue"` (the default), `"cyan"`, `"teal"` or `"green"`. Each event has a border and a bar on its inline-start edge as well as its tint, so it stays visible in forced colors and in print.

### Read-only

Set `readonly: true` on an event to stop the user moving or resizing it. It shows the read-only icon and adds "read-only" to its name. It can still be opened. Set `readonly` on the scheduler to stop creating, moving and resizing events everywhere.

## Create events

Click a slot to pick it, or drag across slots to pick a range. The scheduler highlights the pick and fires `create` with `{ start, end, allDay, trigger }`. Dragging in the all-day row or across days in the month view picks whole days. `end` is exclusive.

`create` is cancelable. Without `preventDefault()` the highlight stays, and `bind:selection` holds the range, so you can open a dialog beside it and set `selection` to `null` when it closes. With `preventDefault()` the highlight is dropped, which suits an app that adds the event at once.

The scheduler never adds the event itself, since only your code knows its title and id.

To create from the keyboard, move to a slot with the arrow keys and press <DocKbd label="Enter" />. <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="Up" /> or <DocKbd label="Down" /> extends the pick to a range.

<FileSource src="/framed/Scheduler/SchedulerCreate" />

## Change events

Drag an event to move it, and drag its bottom edge to resize it. Times snap to `snapMinutes` (default `15`). The scheduler fires `change` with `{ event, start, end, allDay, kind, trigger }`, where `kind` is `"move"` or `"resize"`.

`change` is cancelable. Unless you call `preventDefault()`, the scheduler replaces the event in `events` with a copy that has the new times, so `bind:events` stays current. Cancel the change to reject it, or to wait for a server before updating `events` yourself. <DocKbd label="Escape" /> during a drag cancels it with no event.

A moved event keeps the time that passes between its start and its end. Moving a one-hour event over a DST change leaves it an hour long, even when the wall clock jumps.

<FileSource src="/framed/Scheduler/SchedulerValidate" />

With the keyboard, focus an event and press <DocKbd label="Alt" /> + <DocKbd label="Up" /> or <DocKbd label="Down" /> to move it by one snap step, <DocKbd label="Alt" /> + <DocKbd label="Left" /> or <DocKbd label="Right" /> to move it a day, and <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="Up" /> or <DocKbd label="Down" /> to move its end. An all-day event extends or shortens by a day with <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="Left" /> or <DocKbd label="Right" />. Each key press fires `change` with `trigger: "keyboard"`.

## Time

### Time zone

Event dates are instants. The `timeZone` prop, an IANA name such as `"America/New_York"`, decides which day and clock time each one falls on, so a team in Berlin can look at a calendar in Los Angeles time. It defaults to the browser's own zone. The scheduler reads zones through `Intl`, so it adds no dependency.

### Daylight saving time

The grid always shows the 24 wall-clock hours, so the columns line up. On a day the clocks change, the day is 23 or 25 hours long:

| Day | What the grid shows |
| --- | --- |
| Spring forward (23 hours) | The skipped hour is hatched and nothing can start in it. An event that spans it is taller than its length, since the grid follows the wall clock. |
| Fall back (25 hours) | The repeated hour shows once. An event inside it keeps at least one slot of height. The column's name says it is a 25 hour day. |

Times in the repeated hour belong to the first occurrence, and times in the skipped hour land after it, as `Temporal`'s default does. Moving an event never changes how long it lasts.

<Scheduler events={dstEvents} view="day" date={new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 10, 1, 17))} timeZone="America/New_York" scrollHour={0} height="22rem" />

### Locale and clock

`locale` sets the names and the clock. The week starts on the locale's first day, which comes from the same CLDR table as the [DatePicker](/components/DatePicker); set `weekStartsOn` (`0` for Sunday) to override it. `hourFormat` is `"auto"`, `"12"` or `"24"`.

<FileSource src="/framed/Scheduler/SchedulerLocale" />

## Layout

`slotMinutes` sets the minutes a row covers, from `5` to `60`, and `snapMinutes` the step a drag snaps to. `height` sets the scrolling grid's height, and `--ccs-scheduler-slot-height` the height of a row. The header and the all-day row stay in view as the grid scrolls. Below the `md` breakpoint a week keeps readable columns and scrolls sideways, so use the day view on phones.

The line that marks the current time appears after the page loads, so server-rendered HTML matches the first client render. Set `nowIndicator` to `false` to hide it.

## Accessibility

Each day is a group named by its date, such as "Tuesday, October 27, 2026, today", with a list of its events. Each event is a button named by its title, times and date: "Standup, 9:00 AM to 9:30 AM, Tuesday, October 27, 2026". Use `eventLabelText`, `dayText` and `slotText` to change the wording, for example to translate it.

The month view is a grid: each day is a cell in a row.

Keyboard:

- <DocKbd label="Tab" /> enters the grid on one day, which has a visible cursor, and then reaches that day's events.
- <DocKbd label="Up" /> and <DocKbd label="Down" /> move the cursor by a slot, or between a day's events when one has focus. In the month view they move by a week.
- <DocKbd label="Left" /> and <DocKbd label="Right" /> move to the previous or next day. They swap in right-to-left languages. Moving past the shown range changes `date`.
- <DocKbd label="Home" /> and <DocKbd label="End" /> go to the first and last day of the week.
- <DocKbd label="Page Up" /> and <DocKbd label="Page Down" /> go to the previous or next period.
- <DocKbd label="Enter" /> or <DocKbd label="Space" /> opens the focused event, or creates at the cursor.

The scheduler announces the slot under the cursor and the result of a keyboard move through a live region.

A pointer press on a slot or an event is captured, so a drag keeps working when the pointer leaves the grid. Touch scrolls the page: tap a slot to pick it and an event to open it. Moving and resizing by touch is not supported yet.

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Give every event a unique `id` | The scheduler finds an event by `id` for focus, drag and its keys. |
| Pass `end` as the first instant after the event | A one-hour meeting ending at 11:00 and one starting at 11:00 then never overlap. |
| Pass a fixed `date` when you render on the server | The default is the time the component is created, which can differ between the server and the browser. |
| Keep `events` in one array and use `bind:events`, or cancel `change` | Updating `events` in a `change` handler as well as binding it applies a move twice. |
